    "created_at": "2021-03-30T20:32:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-30T20:33:49Z",
    "body": "@dcrousso the property [[Get]] order, as bzbarsky mentioned, does expose the inheritance chain to ES code. Within a single \"tier\", keys are sorted lexically, but the access order is one-tier-at-a-time. If they were always sorted across the chain, the exposure would go away, but that likely isn't web compatible (and might lead to problems for implementers).\r\n\r\nOne ordering solution for mixins would be to handle them like partials: \"these keys belong to the includes-target, so they get sorted lexically among the others\". I'm pretty sure that would keep the access order well-defined without borking anything that already exists?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
